						<tr>
							<td height="50" colspan="3" valign="top" class="windowbg2" align="left">Naithein, I&#039;m not trying to flame you...just trying to point out that things could always be worse.&nbsp; Perhaps by your babysitting efforts and other ways to save, your mom was able to put aside a few dollars to buy you a Christmas gift...Parents are strange like that, just give your mom some credit.&nbsp; She obviously loves you.&nbsp; Big hugs for thinking about your siblings, I&#039;m sure your mom realizes what a big sacrifice you&#039;re attempting to make and when things get better, you&#039;ll be rewarded accordingly.<br /><br />Colleen, I feel your pain also.&nbsp; Some years it&#039;s been kinda meager in my life also, but it does go in phases.&nbsp; What&#039;s important to realize is that you have a beautiful baby girl to share Christmas with this year.&nbsp; Watch Christmas from her eyes.&nbsp; The colors of the lights, the music and the overall caring this season tends to provide.&nbsp; It might seem strange, but some of the best Christmas&#039; I&#039;ve had were spent watching my children&#039;s anticipation and excitement.&nbsp; With the exception of a handful of gifts, I can&#039;t for the life of me, remember what material gifts I got for Christmas from year to year, but I can, to this day point out the exact individual location of where each of my four kids noticed the lights for the first time, their first and subsequent reactions to Santa Claus and the awesome squeals that come at 5 a.m. in the morning when the kids realized that Santa visited.&nbsp; As far as the bills, don&#039;t sweat the small stuff!&nbsp; After all, you&#039;re not exactly responsible for paying the National Debt.<br /><br />Christmas is about FAMILY not about how many gifts you get and from whom.&nbsp; How many of us wouldn&#039;t give everything we possess for just one minute with a loved one that has passed on?&nbsp; Share the joy of the season with the ones you love and care about!</td>
						</tr>
